# .public-deny — the HARD FUSE. Anything matched here can NEVER reach the
# public mirror, even if it is also (accidentally) on .public-allow.
#
# This is defense-in-depth, not the primary control (deny-by-default already
# keeps unlisted files private). It exists so a careless allow-line for a
# broad glob (e.g. `src/**`) still cannot drag a secret or the core IP out.
#
# Keep this list blunt and permanent. Add categories, not one-offs.

# ── Secrets / credentials (must never be public, period) ──
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*secret*
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/id_rsa*

# ── Core intellectual property: the matching algorithm & its weights ──
src/core/neurotype_matcher.py
src/services/matching_service.py

# ── Internal-only docs (honest status, roadmap, internal summaries) ──
README.internal.md
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
REPOSITORY_SUMMARY.md
docs/PUBLIC_MIRROR.md
